// Placement turns the contact solver into something predictable by hand.
//
// Until a body could be put at a stated spot, the only scenario available
// against the solver was "walk into a grid of 64 and see what happens", which
// can assert that contacts occurred but not where anything ended up. One body
// at a known place makes the whole interaction arithmetic.
//
// The prediction, from the constants rather than from a previous run:
//
//   contact distance = PLAYER_RADIUS + ENEMY_RADIUS = 0.3 + 0.25 = 0.55
//   one tick of walking = PLAYER_SPEED * Dt::SECS  = 9.0 / 60 = 0.15
//   mass split          = 0.05 : 1.0, so the player takes 1/21 of each
//                         correction and the body takes 20/21
//
// Ticks 1-16 are free travel: the player reaches 2.40 and the gap is 0.60,
// still clear of 0.55.
//
// Tick 17 makes contact: the player walks to 2.55, leaving a 0.45 gap and a
// 0.10 overlap. Separation corrects that overlap *in full* — see
// `pass::separate` — so afterwards the gap is exactly 0.55, and stays exactly
// 0.55 every tick after. That is the load-bearing detail: a solver correcting
// some fraction per tick would leave a gap that drifts, and this file would
// fail with a number that says by how much.
//
//   player  2.55  - 0.10/21   = 2.5452381
//   body    3.00  + 0.10*20/21 = 3.0952381
//
// From tick 18 on, both advance 0.15 * 20/21 = 0.1428571 per tick, because the
// player is pushed back by exactly the share of its own step it hands over.
// Thirteen more ticks is 1.8571429:
//
//   player  2.5452381 + 1.8571429 = 4.4023810
//   body    3.0952381 + 1.8571429 = 4.9523810
//
// The tolerance is 0.001 — a hundred and fiftieth of one tick of walking — so
// it absorbs f32 accumulation and nothing else. A tolerance wide enough to hide
// a one-tick error would be the assertion switched off.
(
    description: "A body placed in the player's path is shoved exactly as far as the mass split says.",
    setup: (
        actions: [
            Place((3.0, 0.0)),
        ],
    ),
    inputs: [
        (at: 0, ticks: 30, dir: (1.0, 0.0)),
    ],
    budget: (ticks: 30),
    expect: (
        player_pos: (x: 4.4023810, z: 0.0, tol: 0.001),
        contacts: 1,
        enemy_count: 1,
        bodies: [
            (nth: 0, alive: true, pos: (x: 4.9523810, z: 0.0, tol: 0.001)),
        ],
    ),
)
